module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- The Pattern algebra in Fenel — Brzozowski derivatives over `List a` lifted
-- to a PARSER (named-production recursion + value-carrying reductions + the
-- strict whole-grammar token step + least-fixpoint nullability). parser-
-- substrate Phase 1 (brief:
-- `workstreams/parser-substrate/briefs/phase-1-pattern-algebra.md`).
--
-- This is the algorithmic heart of the parser port. The shipped TS algebra
-- (`engine/src/pattern.ts`) is a boolean recognizer + structured capture,
-- generic over tokens, full SetExpr per element — it is the DIFFERENTIAL
-- ORACLE on the shared fragment (match/seq/alt/rep over enum/interval
-- predicates). What parsing needs and the TS algebra lacks, this file adds:
--
--   • reduction nodes (`PRed` — a Fenel lambda VALUE) + value-carrying eps
--     (`PEpsV` — Might & Darais ε-with-a-tree, single-valued);
--   • named-production recursion (`PRef` + a threaded `Grammar` assoc-list
--     env) — left/mutual recursion that the strict step makes TERMINATE;
--   • least-fixpoint nullability + parseNull (probe-5-proven the genuine
--     hard bit: naive non-recursive nullability is UNSOUND);
--   • `wsMember` — the missing Ws-marker membership decider (`WsWhere ⇒
--     false`, the TS conservative-false posture exactly);
--   • compaction via smart constructors (`mkRed (PEpsV v) f = PEpsV (f v)`
--     is the load-bearing one).
--
-- SINGLE-RESULT (NO parse forest) — Fenel's grammar is unambiguous; first
-- `Just` wins on `PAlt` (P0-locked).
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- DON'T CONFLATE THE TWO `Pattern`s. The match-pattern ADT (`fenel/std/
-- syntax.fenel`, expr-substrate P1) owns the name `Pattern`. The algebra ADT
-- HERE is `Pat` (distinct on purpose); the threaded production env is the
-- assoc list `[{ name, pat }]` (informally "Grammar").
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- PREDICATES = Ws MARKERS (the `$`-key barrier — a `.fenel` body cannot
-- author `$`-prefixed-key objects, so `PMatch` carries a plain-record `Ws*`
-- marker, NOT a `$`-keyed SetExpr — the same vocabulary `solve.fenel` builds
-- and `enumerate.fenel`'s `setExtension` reads). The decidable fragment:
--   { tag = "WsAll" }                       — universe (everything matches)
--   { tag = "WsNone" }                      — empty
--   { tag = "WsEnum", values = [v, …] }     — finite (eq-scan)
--   { tag = "WsPrefix", prefix = "num\0" }  — string PREFIX (startsWith) — the
--                                             7g perf refinement: a value class
--                                             whose membership is "this token's
--                                             TYPE tag is <cls>" is `startsWith x
--                                             "<cls>\0"` (O(prefix)), NOT a
--                                             per-input `WsEnum` eq-scan over the
--                                             whole group's vocabulary (O(group)).
--                                             Semantics-identical on the actual
--                                             input alphabet (a token is in
--                                             `vocabFor toks cls` ⟺ its encoded
--                                             form starts with `cls\0`); see the
--                                             Design-E note in expr-grammar.fenel.
--   { tag = "WsInterval", lo = MB, hi = MB } — MB = Maybe { value, inclusive }
--   { tag = "WsUnion", branches = [Ws, …] } — ∪
--   { tag = "WsIntersect", branches = [Ws, …] } — ∩
--   { tag = "WsComplement", inner = Ws }    — ¬
--   { tag = "WsWhere" }                     — out-of-fragment ⇒ false (the TS
--                                             `contains`→conservative-false)
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- THE STRICT WHOLE-GRAMMAR TOKEN STEP (no laziness anywhere — decision 5).
-- Deriving w.r.t. a token rebuilds the env in ONE finite pass: every
-- production reachable from the current pattern gets a derived sibling whose
-- body is `derivPat` of its old body, where `derivPat (PRef m) = PRef m` — a
-- ref to the (separately) derived production, NO recursion into refs. THAT is
-- what makes left-recursion terminate strictly. Nullability consulted during
-- the PSeq derivative reads the OLD env's fixpoint (`na`/`pa` threaded).
-- Reachability-prune each step (only reachable productions are derived).
--
-- This implementation names derived productions by their LINEAGE `base@birth`
-- (bounded, O(1)-length — parser-substrate 7h): the FIRST time an original
-- `base` is referenced (step k) it spawns `base@k`; on every later step that
-- lineage is re-derived UNDER THE SAME NAME (`bumpName` is idempotent on a name
-- already carrying `@`). The originals stay live, un-derived, so a kept tail's
-- `PRef base` re-enters a FRESH `base@k'`. Distinct lineages (`Expr@6` vs
-- `Expr@7`, born at different steps) stay distinct — they are genuinely
-- different parse states. The pre-7h version appended the WHOLE step history
-- (`base@b1@b2@…@k`), an O(k)-long name; the bounded name shortens it. (S0 read
-- the O(k) name as the dominant super-linear term, but S1a's measurement showed
-- `eq` short-circuits so the name length is NOT the dominant cost — the floor is
-- the linearly-growing `|g|` × the O(|g|) linear-scan env lookups. 7h S2 attacks
-- THAT floor: every name-keyed lookup (`findEntry`-backed `lookupBool`/`lookupVal`/
-- `bodyOf`) + the reachability/prune membership tests now read a `fromEntries`-built
-- name→value INDEX via the O(1) `mapGet` native (the opaque-map perf branch, Rom-
-- approved lever B) — the pure assoc-list stays the source of truth, the JS-object
-- index is its perf rep, so the per-step cost drops O(|g|²) ⇒ ~O(|g|) and the corpus
-- curve cubic ⇒ ~quadratic, byte-identically (env names are unique by the
-- bumpName/dedup invariant ⇒ first-match `findEntry` ≡ the index read). Because a
-- re-derived `base@birth` now shares its name with its prior-step row,
-- `stepGrammarWith` DEDUPS the carried-forward env BY NAME (newSibs-first), which
-- drops ONLY the superseded duplicates — the originals AND any prior derivative a
-- kept tail still re-enters are carried forward intact. (parser-substrate Phase 8
-- then ELIMINATES the dead `∅` rows this leaves reachable through opaque `PRef`s —
-- see "Empty-language ELIMINATION" below — bounding `|g|` from O(k) rows to
-- O(grammar), so the total parse goes ~LINEAR: it closes the 7h-S2 residual
-- quadratic, native-free + byte-identical. The decisive S0 measurement that found
-- this — distinct structural shapes plateau while `|g|` grows O(k), 44% dead rows
-- — is in `workstreams/parser-substrate/notes/phase-8-feasibility.md`.)
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- FIXPOINTS = bounded Kleene iteration over the env, threaded (decision 6).
-- `nullableFix` (Bool lattice, start all-false) and `parseNullFix` (Maybe-
-- value lattice, start all-Nothing, first-Just-wins). Both monotone over a
-- finite env ⇒ converge in ≤ |g| steps; we iterate `|g| + 1` (total, no
-- equality-probe needed). first-Just-wins is deterministic: PAlt tries the
-- left branch first and the recursive branch of a left-recursive production
-- is non-nullable, so a production never flips Just→Just'.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE FROM TS `mkSeq` (recognizer-only): TS collapses
-- `seq eps b = b`. Here `mkSeq` collapses ONLY the `PEmpty` annihilations and
-- KEEPS `PEps`/`PEpsV`, because the parse VALUE depends on the pair nesting
-- (`PSeq` parseNulls to `{ fst, snd }`). Recognition is unaffected (the
-- language is identical); the differential oracle stays green. The PSeq
-- derivative captures the null value of `a` at DERIVATION time via a red
-- (decision 7) — correctness does NOT rely on a `mkSeq` eps-collapse.
--
-- UNBOUNDED REP: `PRep`'s `max` is a plain number; `-1` (negate 1) is the
-- unbounded sentinel (max ≥ min ≥ 0, so -1 is never a real bound). Mirrors
-- `pattern.ts`'s `Infinity` arithmetic: decrement keeps -1, min floors at 0.
--
-- NO LAWS declared (the algebra's laws — D distributes over alt, etc. — are a
-- later add); obligations stay put. `Pat` IS a registered ADT (decision 2) —
-- so this phase MOVES lock/roster/matrix by a documented entity+fn delta.
-- =========================================================================


-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The algebra ADT. Recursive sub-patterns are typed `Pat`; the opaque slots
-- (`value` / `ws` / `min` / `max` / `fn`) are `a` (unconstrained): `ws` is a
-- Ws marker, `fn` a Fenel lambda value, `value` a parsed tree, min/max
-- numbers. `PRef name` is a String key into the threaded env.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

Pat a =
  PEmpty
  | PEps
  | PEpsV value: a
  | PMatch ws: a
  | PSeq left: Pat a right: Pat a
  | PAlt left: Pat a right: Pat a
  | PRep child: Pat a min: a max: a
  | PRed child: Pat a fn: a
  | PRef name: String


-- =========================================================================
-- wsMember — the decidable Ws-marker membership decider.
-- =========================================================================

@label "Ws member"
@description "Decide `x ∈ ws` over the decidable Ws-marker fragment: WsAll ⇒ true; WsNone/WsWhere ⇒ false (WsWhere is the TS `contains`→conservative-false posture); WsEnum ⇒ eq-scan; WsPrefix ⇒ `startsWith x prefix` (the 7g O(prefix) value-class membership — see the Ws-fragment + Design-E notes); WsInterval ⇒ numeric compare honouring each bound's inclusivity + a missing (Nothing) bound = unbounded that side; WsUnion ⇒ any branch; WsIntersect ⇒ all branches; WsComplement ⇒ negation. The missing membership primitive the Ws vocabulary lacked (solve builds markers, enumerate reads extensions, nobody decided `v ∈ ws`). parser-substrate Phase 1."
@tags "engine" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "set" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
wsMember : (ws: a) -> (x: a) -> Boolean
wsMember ws x =
  if eq ws.tag "WsAll" then true
  else if eq ws.tag "WsNone" then false
  else if eq ws.tag "WsWhere" then false
  else if eq ws.tag "WsEnum" then anyEq ws.values x
  else if eq ws.tag "WsPrefix" then startsWith x ws.prefix
  else if eq ws.tag "WsInterval" then intervalMember ws.lo ws.hi x
  else if eq ws.tag "WsUnion" then anyMember ws.branches x
  else if eq ws.tag "WsIntersect" then allMember ws.branches x
  else if eq ws.tag "WsComplement" then not (wsMember ws.inner x)
  else false

@label "Any eq"
@description "True when some element of `vals` is `eq` to `x` (the WsEnum scan). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
anyEq : (vals: a) -> (x: a) -> Boolean
anyEq vals x =
  case head vals of
    Nothing -> false
    Just v ->
      if eq v x then true
      else
        case tail vals of
          Nothing -> false
          Just rest -> anyEq rest x

@label "Any member"
@description "True when `x` is a wsMember of some branch (WsUnion). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
anyMember : (branches: a) -> (x: a) -> Boolean
anyMember branches x =
  case head branches of
    Nothing -> false
    Just b ->
      if wsMember b x then true
      else
        case tail branches of
          Nothing -> false
          Just rest -> anyMember rest x

@label "All member"
@description "True when `x` is a wsMember of every branch (WsIntersect; empty ⇒ true). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
allMember : (branches: a) -> (x: a) -> Boolean
allMember branches x =
  case head branches of
    Nothing -> true
    Just b ->
      if wsMember b x
      then
        case tail branches of
          Nothing -> true
          Just rest -> allMember rest x
      else false

@label "Interval member"
@description "Decide membership in a WsInterval `lo`/`hi` (each a `Maybe { value, inclusive }`): a Nothing bound is unbounded that side; an inclusive bound uses gte/lte, exclusive uses gt/lt. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
intervalMember : (lo: a) -> (hi: a) -> (x: a) -> Boolean
intervalMember lo hi x = and (lowerOk lo x) (upperOk hi x)

@label "Lower bound ok"
@description "The lower-bound half of intervalMember. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
lowerOk : (lo: a) -> (x: a) -> Boolean
lowerOk lo x =
  case lo of
    Nothing -> true
    Just b -> if b.inclusive then gte x b.value else gt x b.value

@label "Upper bound ok"
@description "The upper-bound half of intervalMember. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
upperOk : (hi: a) -> (x: a) -> Boolean
upperOk hi x =
  case hi of
    Nothing -> true
    Just b -> if b.inclusive then lte x b.value else lt x b.value


-- =========================================================================
-- Smart constructors — compaction on the fly (decision 7).
-- =========================================================================

@label "mkSeq"
@description "Sequencing smart constructor: `PEmpty` on either side annihilates to `PEmpty`. EPS-VALUE COLLAPSE (6b lever-A rule 2): `mkSeq (PEpsV v) b = mkRed b (\\x -> { fst = v, snd = x })` and `mkSeq a (PEpsV v) = mkRed a (\\x -> { fst = x, snd = v })` — a settled left/right factor folds into a reduction over the other side, producing the EXACT `{ fst, snd }` nesting PSeq's parseNull builds (the pair-shape contract every grammar reduction reads). KEEPS bare `PEps` (valueless) as PSeq — only PEpsV appears mid-derivation (PMatch ⇒ PEpsV), so the PEps arms are unreachable (pinned, not assumed). Recognition is identical. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
mkSeq : (a: (Pat Any)) -> (b: (Pat Any)) -> (Pat Any)
mkSeq a b =
  case a of
    PEmpty -> PEmpty
    PEpsV v ->
      case b of
        PEmpty -> PEmpty
        other -> mkRed b (\x -> { fst = v, snd = x })
    other ->
      case b of
        PEmpty -> PEmpty
        PEpsV w -> mkRed a (\x -> { fst = x, snd = w })
        other2 -> PSeq a b

@label "mkAlt"
@description "Alternation smart constructor: a `PEmpty` branch drops out (the other wins); otherwise `PAlt`. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
mkAlt : (a: (Pat Any)) -> (b: (Pat Any)) -> (Pat Any)
mkAlt a b =
  case a of
    PEmpty -> b
    other ->
      case b of
        PEmpty -> a
        other2 -> PAlt a b

@label "mkRed"
@description "Reduction smart constructor: `mkRed PEmpty f = PEmpty`; `mkRed (PEpsV v) f = PEpsV (f v)` (THE load-bearing eager compaction); `mkRed (PRed c g) f = mkRed c (\\x -> f (g x))` (RED-FUSION, 6b lever-A rule 1 — collapses stacked reduction layers so derivation-step PRed chains never accumulate; a plain composition lambda, NOT std:compose, since PRed lambdas-in-Pat are 6a-p3-proven); otherwise `PRed`. Arm order: PEmpty → PEpsV → PRed → catch-all. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
mkRed : (child: (Pat Any)) -> (fn: a) -> (Pat Any)
mkRed child fn =
  case child of
    PEmpty -> PEmpty
    PEpsV v -> PEpsV (fn v)
    PRed c g -> mkRed c (\x -> fn (g x))
    other -> PRed child fn


-- =========================================================================
-- Fixpoint convergence detectors (6b lever-A — the per-token fixpoint cache).
--
-- A0's growth pin (6b) showed compaction (rules 1-2) leaves NODE count ~flat
-- but the dominant per-step cost is the env's two Kleene fixpoints iterating a
-- FIXED `|g| + 1` rounds over a row set that grows ~linearly with input ⇒
-- O(|g|) iterations × O(|g|) rows = O(|g|²) per token = the super-linear curve.
--
-- The fix: STOP as soon as the assumption map stops changing. Standard
-- monotone-lattice convergence — both fixpoints are monotone over a finite
-- lattice (Bool / Maybe-value with first-Just-wins), so a round that produces
-- the same map as its input IS the least fixpoint (the next round is a
-- deterministic function of the same input ⇒ identical) and every later round
-- repeats it. `|g| + 1` stays the hard fuel ceiling (the longest ref chain
-- needs that many rounds), but real grammars settle in ~2-4 rounds regardless,
-- so the per-step fixpoint collapses from O(|g|²) to O(c·|g|), c small. The
-- detector is positional (both maps are `map … g` over the SAME `g`, so same
-- length + order) and cheap: Bool eq for nullability; Just/Nothing PRESENCE eq
-- for parseNull (values never flip Just→Just' — the brief's determinism note —
-- so presence stability ⇒ value stability). This is the 6a-brief "lever 1"
-- (incremental fixpoint), here realised as the soundest possible variant: no
-- stratification invariant, just Kleene early-exit.
-- =========================================================================

@label "Bool map stable"
@description "Positional equality of two `[{ name, val: Bool }]` assumption maps (both built by `map … g` over the same env ⇒ same length + order). True ⇒ the Kleene nullability iteration has converged. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
boolMapStable : (xs: a) -> (ys: a) -> Boolean
boolMapStable xs ys =
  case head xs of
    Nothing -> true
    Just x ->
      case head ys of
        Nothing -> false
        Just y ->
          if eq x.val y.val
          then
            case tail xs of
              Nothing -> true
              Just xr ->
                case tail ys of
                  Nothing -> false
                  Just yr -> boolMapStable xr yr
          else false

@label "Is Just"
@description "True when a Maybe value is `Just _`. Internal helper (parseNull convergence presence test)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
isJustVal : (v: a) -> Boolean
isJustVal v =
  case v of
    Just w -> true
    Nothing -> false

@label "Value map stable"
@description "Positional Just/Nothing-PRESENCE equality of two `[{ name, val: Maybe a }]` assumption maps. Presence stability ⇒ value stability (first-Just-wins, no Just→Just' flip), so this is a sound convergence test for the parseNull Kleene iteration. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
valueMapStable : (xs: a) -> (ys: a) -> Boolean
valueMapStable xs ys =
  case head xs of
    Nothing -> true
    Just x ->
      case head ys of
        Nothing -> false
        Just y ->
          if eq (isJustVal x.val) (isJustVal y.val)
          then
            case tail xs of
              Nothing -> true
              Just xr ->
                case tail ys of
                  Nothing -> false
                  Just yr -> valueMapStable xr yr
          else false


-- =========================================================================
-- Nullability fixpoint (Bool lattice).
-- =========================================================================

@label "Nullable under assume"
@description "Does `pat` match the empty input, given a name→Bool INDEX (a `fromEntries`-built record) for `PRef`s? PEps/PEpsV ⇒ true; PEmpty/PMatch ⇒ false; PSeq ⇒ and; PAlt ⇒ or; PRep ⇒ min==0 or nullable child; PRed ⇒ nullable child; PRef ⇒ the assumption (default false). 7h S2: `idx` is the O(1) `mapGet` index built once at each fixpoint round / step boundary, not the O(|g|) assoc-list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
nullableUnderAssume : (idx: a) -> (pat: (Pat Any)) -> Boolean
nullableUnderAssume idx pat =
  case pat of
    PEmpty -> false
    PEps -> true
    PEpsV v -> true
    PMatch w -> false
    PSeq l r -> and (nullableUnderAssume idx l) (nullableUnderAssume idx r)
    PAlt l r -> or (nullableUnderAssume idx l) (nullableUnderAssume idx r)
    PRep c mn mx -> or (eq mn 0) (nullableUnderAssume idx c)
    PRed c f -> nullableUnderAssume idx c
    PRef n -> lookupBool idx n

@label "Nullable fixpoint"
@description "Bounded Kleene iteration for the Bool nullability fixpoint over the production env `g`: start all-false, iterate `|g| + 1` times (monotone over a finite env ⇒ converged). Returns the stable `[{ name, val }]` assumption map. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
nullableFix : (g: a) -> a
nullableFix g = nullableIter g (map (\e -> { name = e.name, val = false }) g) (add (length g) 1)

@label "Nullable iterate"
@description "One-or-more Kleene steps of the Bool nullability fixpoint, fuel-bounded by `|g|+1` but EARLY-EXITING the moment a round reproduces its input map (converged — 6b lever-A). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
nullableIter : (g: a) -> (assume: a) -> (fuel: a) -> a
nullableIter g assume fuel =
  if eq fuel 0 then assume
  else
    let aidx = fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.val }) assume)
    let next = map (\e -> { name = e.name, val = nullableUnderAssume aidx e.pat }) g
    if boolMapStable assume next then next
    else nullableIter g next (sub fuel 1)

@label "Nullable G"
@description "Does `pat` match the empty input under the env `g`'s nullability fixpoint? The recognizer's accept test. parser-substrate Phase 1."
@tags "engine" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
nullableG : (g: a) -> (pat: (Pat Any)) -> Boolean
nullableG g pat = nullableUnderAssume (fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.val }) (nullableFix g))) pat


-- =========================================================================
-- parseNull fixpoint (Maybe-value lattice, first-Just-wins).
-- =========================================================================

@label "Parse-null under assume"
@description "The value `pat` yields on the empty input (Nothing if it doesn't match empty), given a name→(Maybe a) INDEX (a `fromEntries`-built record). PEps ⇒ Just {} (unit); PEpsV v ⇒ Just v; PEmpty/PMatch ⇒ Nothing; PSeq ⇒ Just { fst, snd } when both sides match empty; PAlt ⇒ first Just; PRep ⇒ Just [] when min==0, else min copies of the child's null value; PRed ⇒ fmap the reduction; PRef ⇒ the assumption (default Nothing). 7h S2: `idx` is the O(1) `mapGet` index, not the O(|g|) assoc-list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
parseNullUnderAssume : (idx: a) -> (pat: (Pat Any)) -> Maybe a
parseNullUnderAssume idx pat =
  case pat of
    PEmpty -> Nothing
    PEps -> Just {}
    PEpsV v -> Just v
    PMatch w -> Nothing
    PSeq l r ->
      case parseNullUnderAssume idx l of
        Nothing -> Nothing
        Just lv ->
          case parseNullUnderAssume idx r of
            Nothing -> Nothing
            Just rv -> Just { fst = lv, snd = rv }
    PAlt l r ->
      case parseNullUnderAssume idx l of
        Just lv -> Just lv
        Nothing -> parseNullUnderAssume idx r
    PRep c mn mx ->
      if eq mn 0 then Just []
      else
        case parseNullUnderAssume idx c of
          Nothing -> Nothing
          Just cv -> Just (replicateList mn cv)
    PRed c f ->
      case parseNullUnderAssume idx c of
        Nothing -> Nothing
        Just cv -> Just (f cv)
    PRef n -> lookupVal idx n

@label "Parse-null fixpoint"
@description "Bounded Kleene iteration for the Maybe-value parseNull fixpoint over the env `g`: start all-Nothing, iterate `|g| + 1` times. first-Just-wins is deterministic (PAlt left-first; the recursive branch is non-nullable). Returns the stable `[{ name, val }]` assumption map. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
parseNullFix : (g: a) -> a
parseNullFix g = parseNullIter g (map (\e -> { name = e.name, val = Nothing }) g) (add (length g) 1)

@label "Parse-null iterate"
@description "One-or-more Kleene steps of the Maybe-value parseNull fixpoint, fuel-bounded by `|g|+1` but EARLY-EXITING the moment a round reproduces its input map's Just/Nothing presence (converged — first-Just-wins ⇒ presence stability is value stability; 6b lever-A). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
parseNullIter : (g: a) -> (assume: a) -> (fuel: a) -> a
parseNullIter g assume fuel =
  if eq fuel 0 then assume
  else
    let aidx = fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.val }) assume)
    let next = map (\e -> { name = e.name, val = parseNullUnderAssume aidx e.pat }) g
    if valueMapStable assume next then next
    else parseNullIter g next (sub fuel 1)

@label "Parse-null G"
@description "The value `pat` yields on the empty input under the env `g`'s parseNull fixpoint (Nothing if it doesn't match empty). The parser's accept-value. parser-substrate Phase 1."
@tags "engine" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
parseNullG : (g: a) -> (pat: (Pat Any)) -> Maybe a
parseNullG g pat = parseNullUnderAssume (fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.val }) (parseNullFix g))) pat

@label "Null value under assume"
@description "The unwrapped null value of `pat` under a name→(Maybe a) INDEX (`{}` when it doesn't match empty — only ever called where nullability is already established, so the default is unobservable). Captures `a`'s null parse at PSeq-derivation time. 7h S2: `idx` is the O(1) `mapGet` index. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
nullValueAssume : (idx: a) -> (pat: (Pat Any)) -> a
nullValueAssume idx pat =
  case parseNullUnderAssume idx pat of
    Just v -> v
    Nothing -> {}

@label "Replicate list"
@description "A list of `n` copies of `v` (n ≤ 0 ⇒ empty). Used for a min>0 PRep's null value. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
replicateList : (n: a) -> (v: a) -> a
replicateList n v =
  if lte n 0 then []
  else appendItem v (replicateList (sub n 1) v)


-- =========================================================================
-- derivPat — the single-result Brzozowski derivative (decision 7).
-- Threads the OLD env's fixpoint maps `na` (Bool) + `pa` (Maybe-value).
-- =========================================================================

@label "Derive pattern"
@description "The single-result Brzozowski derivative of `pat` w.r.t. token `t`, at step suffix `k`, threading the OLD env's nullability (`naIdx`) + parseNull (`paIdx`) fixpoint INDEXES (7h S2: name→value `fromEntries`-built records read O(1) via `mapGet`, built once per step by the caller). PMatch ⇒ PEpsV t when `wsMember`, else PEmpty. PSeq with a nullable left captures the left's null VALUE at derivation time via a red (the M&D `δ(a)∘D(b)` rule); the right tail is KEPT LITERAL so its refs stay pointed at the FRESH (un-derived) productions — that is what lets `\"1\" S \"2\"` re-enter a fresh S. PRef m ⇒ PRef m@k (the derived SIBLING, NOT a recursion into m's body) — the strict-step that makes left/mutual recursion terminate. PRep mirrors `pattern.ts` (min floors at 0, the -1 unbounded sentinel stays -1). parser-substrate Phase 1."
@tags "engine" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "derivative" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
derivPat : (naIdx: a) -> (paIdx: a) -> (t: a) -> (k: a) -> (pat: (Pat Any)) -> (Pat Any)
derivPat naIdx paIdx t k pat =
  case pat of
    PEmpty -> PEmpty
    PEps -> PEmpty
    PEpsV v -> PEmpty
    PMatch w -> if wsMember w t then PEpsV t else PEmpty
    PSeq l r ->
      if nullableUnderAssume naIdx l
      then
        let lv = nullValueAssume paIdx l
        mkAlt (mkSeq (derivPat naIdx paIdx t k l) r) (mkRed (derivPat naIdx paIdx t k r) (\x -> { fst = lv, snd = x }))
      else mkSeq (derivPat naIdx paIdx t k l) r
    PAlt l r -> mkAlt (derivPat naIdx paIdx t k l) (derivPat naIdx paIdx t k r)
    PRep c mn mx ->
      if eq mx 0 then PEmpty
      else mkSeq (derivPat naIdx paIdx t k c) (PRep c (maxNum 0 (sub mn 1)) (decMax mx))
    PRed c f -> mkRed (derivPat naIdx paIdx t k c) f
    PRef n -> PRef (bumpName n k)

@label "Bump name"
@description "The derived-sibling name of production `m` at step `k`, BOUNDED per-lineage (parser-substrate 7h): an ORIGINAL name (no `@`) gets ONE suffix `m@k` — a fresh lineage BORN at step k (the step at which the original was first referenced; re-entry into a fresh production). An ALREADY-derived name (`base@birth`, contains `@`) is returned UNCHANGED — same lineage, one more token consumed under the same stable name. So a derivative is named `base@birth` (O(1) length), NOT the cumulative `base@b1@b2@…@k` chain the pre-7h version appended every step (the O(k)-name-length term that was the dominant super-linear cost — S0 cubic diagnosis). The lineage `(base, birthStep)` is INVARIANT as the derivative consumes tokens, and collision-free: at any step there is exactly ONE live derivative per `(base, birth)` (deriveProductions maps over the deduped reach), and genuinely-distinct lineages (`Expr@6` vs `Expr@7`, born at different steps) stay distinct. Original production names never contain `@`, so the membership test is exact. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
bumpName : (m: String) -> (k: a) -> String
bumpName m k = if elem "@" (chars m) then m else concat (concat m "@") (toString k)

@label "Max number"
@description "Numeric max of two numbers. Internal helper (min-bound floor in the rep derivative)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
maxNum : (a: a) -> (b: a) -> a
maxNum a b = if gt a b then a else b

@label "Decrement max"
@description "Decrement a PRep `max`, keeping the `-1` unbounded sentinel fixed. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
decMax : (mx: a) -> a
decMax mx = if eq mx (negate 1) then negate 1 else sub mx 1


-- =========================================================================
-- The env: lookups + reachability (assoc list `[{ name, pat }]` / `[{ name,
-- val }]`).
-- =========================================================================

@label "Find entry"
@description "Linear scan a `[{ name, … }]` list for the first entry whose `.name` matches; Just it / Nothing. Shared by the grammar (`{ name, pat }`) and the assumption maps (`{ name, val }`). NOTE (7h S2): the hot per-step lookups (lookupBool/lookupVal/bodyOf) no longer go through this O(|g|) scan — they read a `fromEntries`-built name→value INDEX via the O(1) `mapGet` native (the opaque-map perf branch). `findEntry` stays as the general first-match assoc-list primitive (no longer on the parser's hot path). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
findEntry : (items: a) -> (name: String) -> Maybe a
findEntry items name =
  case head items of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just it ->
      if eq it.name name then Just it
      else
        case tail items of
          Nothing -> Nothing
          Just rest -> findEntry rest name

@label "Lookup bool"
@description "The Bool value bound to `name` in a name→Bool INDEX (a `fromEntries`-built record; default false — an unbound PRef is conservatively non-nullable). 7h S2: O(1) `mapGet` read replacing the O(|g|) `findEntry` scan (the env-lookup de-superlinearization — the assoc-list stays the source of truth, this reads its opaque-map index). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
lookupBool : (idx: a) -> (name: String) -> Boolean
lookupBool idx name =
  case mapGet idx name of
    Nothing -> false
    Just v -> v

@label "Lookup val"
@description "The Maybe-value bound to `name` in a name→(Maybe a) INDEX (a `fromEntries`-built record; default Nothing). 7h S2: O(1) `mapGet` read replacing the O(|g|) `findEntry` scan. The stored value is itself a Maybe (the parseNull lattice), so a present key returns that Maybe directly. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
lookupVal : (idx: a) -> (name: String) -> Maybe a
lookupVal idx name =
  case mapGet idx name of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just v -> v

@label "Seed bool map"
@description "Build the seed Bool assumption map for env `g` from a PRIOR step's converged nullability map: an ORIGINAL name (no `@` — an un-derived production whose body NEVER changes) carries forward its prior value (identical body ⇒ identical fixpoint); a DERIVATIVE name (`@`) defaults false (⊥). The seed MUST be ≤ the least fixpoint pointwise (the Kleene iteration only moves UP, so a too-high seed would NOT be corrected). Under bounded `base@birth` naming (7h) a derivative KEEPS its name across steps while its body is RE-DERIVED each step, so carrying its prior value forward would seed the OLD body's fixpoint — generally > the new body's least fixpoint ⇒ UNSOUND (it silently mis-captured a nullable kept-tail's null value — an empty-record argument dropped a trailing arg). Seeding derivatives ⊥ recomputes them from scratch, exactly as the pre-7h cumulative naming did implicitly (a fresh per-step name always looked up ⊥). Originals stay the 6b incremental-fixpoint cache. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
seedBool : (g: a) -> (prior: a) -> a
seedBool g prior =
  let pidx = fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.val }) prior)
  map (\e -> { name = e.name, val = if elem "@" (chars e.name) then false else lookupBool pidx e.name }) g

@label "Seed value map"
@description "Build the seed Maybe-value assumption map for env `g` from a PRIOR step's converged parseNull map: ORIGINAL names (no `@`, stable body) carry forward; DERIVATIVE names (`@`) default Nothing (⊥). Same 7h soundness reason as `seedBool` — under bounded `base@birth` naming a derivative keeps its name while its body is re-derived, so carrying its prior parseNull value forward seeds the OLD body's (too-high) value and the monotone Kleene iteration can't lower it ⇒ a nullable kept-tail captures the wrong null value (the empty-record-arg trailing-arg drop). Seeding derivatives ⊥ recomputes them, as cumulative naming did implicitly. Originals stay the 6b incremental-fixpoint cache. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
seedVal : (g: a) -> (prior: a) -> a
seedVal g prior =
  let pidx = fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.val }) prior)
  map (\e -> { name = e.name, val = if elem "@" (chars e.name) then Nothing else lookupVal pidx e.name }) g

@label "Body of"
@description "The body pattern of production `name` in a name→Pat env INDEX (a `fromEntries`-built record; PEmpty when absent — an unbound ref is dead). 7h S2: O(1) `mapGet` read replacing the O(|g|) `findEntry` scan. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
bodyOf : (gidx: a) -> (name: String) -> (Pat Any)
bodyOf gidx name =
  case mapGet gidx name of
    Nothing -> PEmpty
    Just p -> p

@label "Collect refs"
@description "The list of `PRef` names directly inside `pat` (structural — recurses through Seq/Alt/Rep/Red but NOT through a ref's body, since PRef is a leaf here). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
collectRefs : (pat: (Pat Any)) -> a
collectRefs pat =
  case pat of
    PSeq l r -> concat (collectRefs l) (collectRefs r)
    PAlt l r -> concat (collectRefs l) (collectRefs r)
    PRep c mn mx -> collectRefs c
    PRed c f -> collectRefs c
    PRef n -> [n]
    other -> []

@label "Dedup strings"
@description "Order-preserving de-duplication of a string list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
dedupStr : (xs: a) -> a
dedupStr xs = dedupStrInto xs []

@label "Dedup strings into"
@description "dedupStr's accumulator pass: append each unseen element. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
dedupStrInto : (xs: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
dedupStrInto xs acc =
  case head xs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just h ->
      let acc2 = if elem h acc then acc else appendItem h acc
      case tail xs of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> dedupStrInto rest acc2

@label "Reachable names"
@description "The transitive closure of production names reachable from `root` via `PRef` over env `g` (the reachability-prune frontier of the strict step — only these productions get derived). 7h S2: builds the name→Pat env INDEX once (`fromEntries`) and threads it to the worklist BFS so each `bodyOf` is an O(1) `mapGet`, not an O(|g|) scan. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
reachableNames : (g: a) -> (root: (Pat Any)) -> a
reachableNames g root =
  let gidx = fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.pat }) g)
  let seed = dedupStr (collectRefs root)
  growNames gidx seed seed

@label "Grow names"
@description "Worklist BFS over the reachability graph (6b lever-A — replaces the old whole-accumulator re-scan): `seen` is the accumulated reachable set, `frontier` the names discovered last round. Each round collects refs of ONLY the frontier's bodies (via the env index `gidx`), keeps the unseen ones (`notSeen`), and recurses with them as the new frontier — terminating when nothing fresh appears. 7h S2: `gidx` is the name→Pat index (O(1) bodyOf) and `notSeen` does O(1) set-membership, so a round is O(|frontier|·refs + |seen|) and the BFS is O(diameter·|g|) per step (the wide-shallow grammar's diameter is small) — replacing the prior O(|g|²)-per-step linear scans. No fuel bound needed (seen grows monotonically, bounded by |g|). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
growNames : (gidx: a) -> (seen: a) -> (frontier: a) -> a
growNames gidx seen frontier =
  let fresh = notSeen (dedupStr (refsOfNames gidx frontier)) seen
  case head fresh of
    Nothing -> seen
    Just h -> growNames gidx (concat seen fresh) fresh

@label "Not seen"
@description "The elements of `xs` not already in `seen` (the worklist frontier filter). 7h S2: builds a name→True SET from `seen` (`fromEntries`) once per call, then tests membership O(1) via `mapGet`/`isJustVal` — byte-identical to the prior `elem`-scan filter (same order, same kept elements), just sub-linear. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
notSeen : (xs: a) -> (seen: a) -> a
notSeen xs seen =
  let seenSet = fromEntries (map (\n -> { key = n, value = true }) seen)
  filter (\x -> not (isJustVal (mapGet seenSet x))) xs

@label "Refs of names"
@description "All refs in the bodies of the given production names (concatenated; bodies read from the env INDEX `gidx` via O(1) `bodyOf`). Internal helper for reachability growth."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
refsOfNames : (gidx: a) -> (names: a) -> a
refsOfNames gidx names = refsOfNamesInto gidx names []

@label "Refs of names into"
@description "refsOfNames' accumulator pass: append each production body's refs (body via the env index `gidx`). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
refsOfNamesInto : (gidx: a) -> (names: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
refsOfNamesInto gidx names acc =
  case head names of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just n ->
      let acc2 = concat acc (collectRefs (bodyOf gidx n))
      case tail names of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> refsOfNamesInto gidx rest acc2


-- =========================================================================
-- The strict whole-grammar token step + the driver.
-- =========================================================================

@label "Derive productions"
@description "Derive the bodies of the named (reachable) productions of `g` w.r.t. token `t` at step `k`, threading the fixpoint INDEXES `naIdx`/`paIdx` — the env half of the strict whole-grammar step. 7h S2: builds the env's name→Pat index once (`fromEntries`) so each `bodyOf` is O(1). Each reachable production `n` yields a derived sibling named `n@k`. Returns the new `[{ name, pat }]` siblings. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveProductions : (g: a) -> (naIdx: a) -> (paIdx: a) -> (t: a) -> (k: a) -> (names: a) -> a
deriveProductions g naIdx paIdx t k names =
  let gidx = fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.pat }) g)
  map (\n -> { name = bumpName n k, pat = derivPat naIdx paIdx t k (bodyOf gidx n) }) names


-- =========================================================================
-- Empty-language ELIMINATION — the Phase-8 de-superlinearization that bounds
-- `|g|`. The strict step keeps DEAD (`∅`) productions reachable through opaque
-- `PRef`s that the LOCAL smart constructors (`mkSeq`/`mkAlt`) cannot compact
-- through — so `|g|` grows O(k) in the token count even though the live
-- grammar has only O(grammar) DISTINCT residual languages (Brzozowski
-- finiteness; measured: ~208 rows vs ~60 distinct shapes on a 64-step decl).
-- This pass is the M&D `∅`-compaction this NAMED-production formulation must do
-- explicitly: compute the empty-set fixpoint, simplify every body propagating
-- emptiness (`PRef ∅ ⇒ PEmpty`, so `∅` factors annihilate + `∅` branches drop),
-- drop the empty rows, re-prune reachable. Running it at the TAIL of every step
-- keeps the env that flows to the NEXT step bounded ⇒ `combined` never grows
-- O(k) ⇒ the per-step work is O(grammar) and the total is LINEAR (vs the 7h-S2
-- residual quadratic). Language-and-value preserving (a `∅` production matches
-- nothing + carries no reduction value) ⇒ `parseNull` is byte-identical; only
-- the live grammar shrinks. NO new native — reuses `mkSeq`/`mkAlt`/`mkRed` +
-- the 7h-S2 `mapGet`/`fromEntries` opaque-map index.
-- =========================================================================

@label "Body empty under"
@description "Does `pat` denote the EMPTY language `∅` given a name→true INDEX `empt` of already-known-empty productions? PEmpty ⇒ true; PSeq ⇒ either side empty (`∅·x = ∅`); PAlt ⇒ both sides empty (`∅|∅ = ∅`); PRep ⇒ `∅` only when it REQUIRES ≥1 rep (`mn>0`) AND the child is `∅` (a `mn==0` rep matches ε ⇒ nullable, NOT `∅`; for valid `min≤max` reps `mx==0 ⇒ mn==0`, so the old `mx==0` shortcut wrongly emptied a nullable exhausted bounded-rep — the algebra-differential bug the all-unbounded-rep corpus missed); PRed ⇒ child empty; PRef ⇒ in `empt`; PEps/PEpsV/PMatch ⇒ false (they accept ε-with-value / a token). The boolean (non-allocating) form of `isPEmpty ∘ simplifyEmpty` — used to compute the empty-set without rebuilding trees. Internal helper. parser-substrate Phase 8."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-8"
@category "engine-internal"
bodyEmptyUnder : (empt: a) -> (pat: (Pat Any)) -> Boolean
bodyEmptyUnder empt pat =
  case pat of
    PEmpty -> true
    PSeq l r -> or (bodyEmptyUnder empt l) (bodyEmptyUnder empt r)
    PAlt l r -> and (bodyEmptyUnder empt l) (bodyEmptyUnder empt r)
    PRep c mn mx -> and (gt mn 0) (bodyEmptyUnder empt c)
    PRed c f -> bodyEmptyUnder empt c
    PRef n -> isJustVal (mapGet empt n)
    other -> false

@label "Empty body names"
@description "The names of the productions of `g` whose body is `∅` under the current empty INDEX `empt` (name→true) — one round of the empty-set fixpoint. Internal helper. parser-substrate Phase 8."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-8"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyBodyNames : (g: a) -> (empt: a) -> a
emptyBodyNames g empt =
  map (\e -> e.name) (filter (\e -> bodyEmptyUnder empt e.pat) g)

@label "Empty names iterate"
@description "One-or-more rounds of the empty-set least fixpoint over `g`, fuel-bounded by `|g|+1` (the longest empty-propagation chain) but EARLY-EXITING once a round adds no new empty name. The set is monotone-INCREASING (a larger empty index can only make more bodies empty), so a round of the same length as its input IS the fixpoint. Internal helper. parser-substrate Phase 8."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-8"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyNamesIter : (g: a) -> (prev: a) -> (fuel: a) -> a
emptyNamesIter g prev fuel =
  if eq fuel 0 then prev
  else
    let empt = fromEntries (map (\n -> { key = n, value = true }) prev)
    let cur = emptyBodyNames g empt
    if eq (length cur) (length prev) then cur
    else emptyNamesIter g cur (sub fuel 1)

@label "Empty names fixpoint"
@description "The least fixpoint of empty (`∅`) production names of `g`: start with none, iterate `emptyNamesIter` to convergence. Internal helper. parser-substrate Phase 8."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-8"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyNamesFix : (g: a) -> a
emptyNamesFix g = emptyNamesIter g [] (add (length g) 1)

@label "Simplify empty"
@description "Rewrite a body PROPAGATING emptiness through references: a `PRef n` whose production is in the empty INDEX `empt` (name→true) becomes `PEmpty`, and the smart constructors re-fire bottom-up so `∅` factors annihilate (`mkSeq ∅ = ∅`) and `∅` branches drop (`mkAlt ∅ x = x`, preserving first-Just-wins since a `∅` branch never yields a Just). `PRep` just recurses into its child (NO `mx==0` collapse — that would wrongly empty a nullable exhausted rep; a genuinely-`∅` rep, `mn>0` over a `∅` child, is caught by `bodyEmptyUnder` at the production level + the row-drop). Only called in the elimination's empty-present branch (the common empty-free step keeps the OLD reachability prune verbatim). Language-and-value preserving. Internal helper. parser-substrate Phase 8."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-8"
@category "engine-internal"
simplifyEmpty : (empt: a) -> (pat: (Pat Any)) -> (Pat Any)
simplifyEmpty empt pat =
  case pat of
    PSeq l r -> mkSeq (simplifyEmpty empt l) (simplifyEmpty empt r)
    PAlt l r -> mkAlt (simplifyEmpty empt l) (simplifyEmpty empt r)
    PRep c mn mx -> PRep (simplifyEmpty empt c) mn mx
    PRed c f -> mkRed (simplifyEmpty empt c) f
    PRef n -> if isJustVal (mapGet empt n) then PEmpty else PRef n
    other -> other

@label "Eliminate empty"
@description "The empty-language ELIMINATION pass that bounds `|g|` (parser-substrate Phase 8). Compute the empty-set fixpoint of `g`; when EMPTY (the common case) keep the OLD reachability prune over `(g, root)` VERBATIM (byte-identical to the pre-8 `stepGrammarWith` tail). When there ARE empties: simplify the root + every kept body propagating them (refs to `∅` annihilate via the smart constructors), DROP the empty rows, and re-prune to the productions reachable from the simplified root. Returns `{ g, root }`. Sound — a `∅` production contributes to no accepting parse and carries no reduction value, so the residual root's `parseNull` is byte-identical; only the live grammar shrinks from O(k) rows to O(grammar). Internal helper. parser-substrate Phase 8."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-8"
@category "engine-internal"
eliminateEmpty : (g: a) -> (root: (Pat Any)) -> a
eliminateEmpty g root =
  let emptNames = emptyNamesFix g
  if eq (length emptNames) 0
  then
    let keepNames = reachableNames g root
    let keepSet = fromEntries (map (\n -> { key = n, value = true }) keepNames)
    { g = filter (\e -> isJustVal (mapGet keepSet e.name)) g, root = root }
  else
    let empt = fromEntries (map (\n -> { key = n, value = true }) emptNames)
    let root2 = simplifyEmpty empt root
    let kept = filter (\e -> not (isJustVal (mapGet empt e.name))) g
    let g1 = map (\e -> { name = e.name, pat = simplifyEmpty empt e.pat }) kept
    let keepNames = reachableNames g1 root2
    let keepSet = fromEntries (map (\n -> { key = n, value = true }) keepNames)
    { g = filter (\e -> isJustVal (mapGet keepSet e.name)) g1, root = root2 }

@label "Step grammar with"
@description "The core strict whole-grammar derivative step at suffix `k`, taking the OLD env's PRECOMPUTED nullability (`na`) + parseNull (`pa`) fixpoints (so the caller can thread them incrementally across steps — the 6b cache). Derive the root + every reachable production w.r.t. `t` in one finite pass into bounded `base@birth` siblings (refs bump to the derived siblings; kept tails retain their fresh refs — so left/mutual recursion terminate AND re-enter fresh productions). The new env = `newSibs` ++ (the old env MINUS any row a newSib supersedes). DEDUP-BY-NAME, newSibs-first (7h): under bounded naming a re-derived `base@birth` shares its name with its prior-step row, so the naive `concat newSibs g` would carry BOTH (the fresh + the one-step-stale) and re-leak `|g|` — `findEntry`/`bodyOf` would still pick the fresh (first) one, but the stale copy bloats every per-step scan. Dropping ONLY the colliding old rows (those whose name is a newSib name) is correct AND complete: newSibs holds the freshest derivative of every reachable production, while the NON-colliding old rows (the originals the kept tails re-enter, PLUS any prior-step derivative NOT re-derived this step but still referenced by a kept tail — e.g. a multi-argument application's later-argument re-entry) MUST be carried forward (an earlier 7h draft that kept only the non-`@` originals dropped exactly those tails and lost a trailing call argument). With cumulative (pre-7h) names no row ever collided, so this is a no-op there — i.e. semantically identical to the old `concat newSibs g`, plus the bounded-name dedup. Then keep the rows still reachable from the new root, prune the rest. 7h S2 (env-lookup de-superlinearization): the OLD env's `na`/`pa` fixpoints arrive as the threaded assoc-lists and are indexed ONCE here (`naIdx`/`paIdx`, O(1) `mapGet`) for the whole step; the two row prunes (`combined`'s drop-superseded + `g2`'s keep-reachable) use name→True SETS (`newNamesSet`/`keepSet`) for O(1) membership instead of the prior O(|g|) `elem` scans — so the per-step cost drops from O(|g|²) to ~O(|g|) and the corpus curve from cubic toward quadratic. Returns `{ g, root }`. parser-substrate Phase 1 / 6b / 7h. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1" "phase-7h"
@category "engine-internal"
stepGrammarWith : (g: a) -> (root: (Pat Any)) -> (t: a) -> (k: a) -> (na: a) -> (pa: a) -> a
stepGrammarWith g root t k na pa =
  let naIdx = fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.val }) na)
  let paIdx = fromEntries (map (\e -> { key = e.name, value = e.val }) pa)
  let reach = reachableNames g root
  let newSibs = deriveProductions g naIdx paIdx t k reach
  let root2 = derivPat naIdx paIdx t k root
  let newNames = map (\e -> e.name) newSibs
  let newNamesSet = fromEntries (map (\n -> { key = n, value = true }) newNames)
  let combined = concat newSibs (filter (\e -> not (isJustVal (mapGet newNamesSet e.name))) g)
  -- parser-substrate Phase 8: the reachability prune AND the empty-language
  -- elimination that bounds `|g|` (drops the dead `∅` rows the strict step keeps
  -- reachable through opaque PRefs — the residual quadratic 7h-S2 banked). On a
  -- step with no empties this is the OLD prune VERBATIM (byte-identical);
  -- otherwise it shrinks the carried env from O(k) rows toward O(grammar), so the
  -- env flowing to the next step stays bounded ⇒ the total parse goes LINEAR.
  eliminateEmpty combined root2

@label "Step grammar"
@description "One strict whole-grammar derivative step at suffix `k`, computing the OLD env's fixpoints fresh then delegating to `stepGrammarWith`. The back-compat entry (the lexer's ref-free empty-env driver + the env-growth oracle call it; the grammar path uses the threaded `runSteps`). parser-substrate Phase 1."
@tags "engine" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
stepGrammar : (g: a) -> (root: (Pat Any)) -> (t: a) -> (k: a) -> a
stepGrammar g root t k = stepGrammarWith g root t k (nullableFix g) (parseNullFix g)

@label "Run steps"
@description "Fold the strict token step over an input list, threading `{ g, root }`, an incrementing step suffix `k`, AND the OLD env's nullability/parseNull fixpoints (`na`/`pa`) — the 6b INCREMENTAL-FIXPOINT cache: after each step the next env's fixpoints are reseeded from the prior converged maps (kept rows carry forward, fresh `@k` rows default ⊥) and re-converged by early-exit Kleene in a few frontier rounds, instead of recomputed from ⊥ over the deepening chain (O(|g|²) ⇒ O(|g|) per step). Short-circuits once the root is PEmpty (dead). parser-substrate Phase 1 / 6b."
@tags "engine" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
runSteps : (g: a) -> (root: (Pat Any)) -> (k: a) -> (toks: a) -> (na: a) -> (pa: a) -> a
runSteps g root k toks na pa =
  case head toks of
    Nothing -> { g = g, root = root }
    Just t ->
      case root of
        PEmpty -> { g = g, root = PEmpty }
        other ->
          let stepped = stepGrammarWith g root t k na pa
          case tail toks of
            Nothing -> stepped
            Just rest ->
              let na2 = nullableIter stepped.g (seedBool stepped.g na) (add (length stepped.g) 1)
              let pa2 = parseNullIter stepped.g (seedVal stepped.g pa) (add (length stepped.g) 1)
              runSteps stepped.g stepped.root (add k 1) rest na2 pa2

@label "Recognize G"
@description "Does the token list `toks` match production `start` of grammar `g`? Folds the strict whole-grammar derivative over `toks` (suffixes start at 1, fixpoints threaded incrementally), then tests nullability of the residual root under the residual env. Single-result; left/mutual recursion terminate. The differential oracle wraps a ref-free root as a singleton grammar. parser-substrate Phase 1."
@tags "engine" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "recognizer" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
recognizeG : (g: a) -> (start: String) -> (toks: a) -> Boolean
recognizeG g start toks =
  let final = runSteps g (PRef start) 1 toks (nullableFix g) (parseNullFix g)
  nullableG final.g final.root

@label "Parse G"
@description "Parse the token list `toks` against production `start` of grammar `g`, returning the reduced value (`Just value` on a full match, Nothing otherwise). Folds the strict derivative over `toks` (fixpoints threaded incrementally), then reads the residual root's parseNull value under the residual env — so reductions (`PRed`) build a real `Syntax`-shaped tree end-to-end. parser-substrate Phase 1."
@tags "engine" "parser" "pattern-algebra" "parser" "parser-substrate" "phase-1"
parseG : (g: a) -> (start: String) -> (toks: a) -> Maybe a
parseG g start toks =
  let final = runSteps g (PRef start) 1 toks (nullableFix g) (parseNullFix g)
  parseNullG final.g final.root
